{"key":"enterprise/T1137.006","id":"T1137.006","name":"Add-ins","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1137","tactics":["persistence"],"platforms":["Windows","Office Suite"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may abuse Microsoft Office add-ins to obtain persistence on a compromised system. Office add-ins can be used to add functionality to Office programs. There are different types of add-ins that can be used by the various Office products; including Word/Excel add-in Libraries (WLL/XLL), VBA add-ins, Office Component Object Model (COM) add-ins, automation add-ins, VBA Editor (VBE), Visual Studio Tools for Office (VSTO) add-ins, and…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1137/006","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--34f1d81d-fe88-4f97-bd3b-a3164536255d","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:37.911Z","source_object_version":"1.2","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0038","name":"Application Log Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0038","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9c2fa0ae-7abc-485a-97f6-699e3b6cf9fa","page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0063","name":"Windows Registry Key Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0063","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--da85d358-741a-410d-9433-20d6269a6170","page":"telemetry/DC0063/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0050","name":"Detect Persistence via Malicious Office Add-ins","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0050","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--53144b02-d6b1-42de-b5cf-e785a59c43bd","relationship_id":"relationship--ce52ceb4-fced-4ec9-8e0a-8c1a1f871a64"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0137","name":"Analytic 0137","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0050#AN0137","guidance":"An adversary writes or drops a malicious Office Add-in (e.g., WLL, XLL, COM) to a trusted directory or modifies registry keys to load malicious add-ins on Office application launch. Upon user opening Word or Excel, the add-in is automatically loaded, triggering execution of the payload, often spawning scripting engines or anomalous child processes.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0050"},{"id":"AN0138","name":"Analytic 0138","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0050#AN0138","guidance":"Malicious Office add-ins loaded via VSTO, COM, or VBA auto-load paths. Upon launch of Word/Excel/Outlook, the add-in executes code without user action. Add-in resides in trusted directory or registered via Office COM/VBE subsystem. Behavior includes unsigned add-in execution, anomalous load context, or add-in spawning interpreter process.","platforms":["Office Suite"],"strategy_id":"DET0050"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0137","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0050#AN0137","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0039","component":"File Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"